<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>TriTrack</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/</link><description>Recent content on TriTrack</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Quick start</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/quick-start/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/quick-start/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Six steps, in order. The first time you open TriTrack it asks for your name&#10;and email, which label everything you record.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="1-create-the-project"&gt;1. Create the project&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10;, then &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Projects&lt;/b&gt;&#10;, and tap the + button at&#10;the bottom right. Give it a &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Name&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;SAVE PROJECT&lt;/b&gt;&#10;;&#10;it becomes the open project. More in&#10;&lt;a href="../projects-members-and-roles/"&gt;projects, members and roles&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="2-add-the-animals-and-their-tags"&gt;2. Add the animals and their tags&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;On &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; → &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Animals&lt;/b&gt;&#10;, tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Quick add&lt;/b&gt;&#10;. Set&#10;the day the tags went on once, at the top, then type one row per animal: its&#10;name and its frequency, or paste the rows from a spreadsheet. A frequency that&#10;matches no tag on the project or in your Tag Library becomes a new tag. Nothing&#10;is saved until you tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Review&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and then the add button under it.&#10;More in &lt;a href="../managing-your-tags/#putting-a-tag-on-an-animal"&gt;putting a tag on an animal&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Joining a project</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/joining-a-project/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/joining-a-project/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Joining needs a connection, both to ask and for the answer to come back, so do&#10;it before you lose signal. Everything after that works offline.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="sign-in"&gt;Sign in&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; → &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Server Connection&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and enter the server&#10;address you were given. Tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;REQUEST A SIGN-IN CODE&lt;/b&gt;&#10; with your&#10;email, then paste the code, or the whole link, into &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Sign-in code&lt;/b&gt;&#10;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;How the code reaches you depends on the server&lt;/em&gt;, and the app cannot know. If&#10;nothing arrives, ask whoever runs the server how codes are delivered.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Projects, members and roles</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/projects-members-and-roles/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/projects-members-and-roles/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Everything you record belongs to a project. A phone can hold several; the one&#10;with the green tick under &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; → &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Projects&lt;/b&gt;&#10; is open.&#10;Tap a name to open it. Your &lt;a href="../managing-your-tags/"&gt;Tag Library&lt;/a&gt; belongs to the&#10;phone, not to any project.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/joined-projects.png" alt="The projects list on an owner&amp;#39;s device. The tick marks the active project, Join a project sits above the list, and everything you can do to a project is behind the three-dot button at the end of its row." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;The projects list on an owner&amp;#39;s device. The tick marks the active project, Join a project sits above the list, and everything you can do to a project is behind the three-dot button at the end of its row.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The three-dot button on a row holds &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Publish to server&lt;/b&gt;&#10; (before a&#10;project is on a server), &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Members&lt;/b&gt;&#10;,&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Edit project&lt;/b&gt;&#10;, &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Start next season&lt;/b&gt;&#10;,&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Leave project&lt;/b&gt;&#10; (once on a server) and, last,&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Delete project&lt;/b&gt;&#10;. An entry your role does not allow stays in the&#10;menu, grayed, with the reason under it, for example&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Only a project owner can delete this project.&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Recording a bearing</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/recording-a-bearing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/recording-a-bearing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Pick the tag, point the antenna, take the bearing, save.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/record.png" alt="The Record tab, ready to take a bearing. The round button with a map on it, beside RANGE, is Take on map." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;The Record tab, ready to take a bearing. The round button with a map on it, beside RANGE, is Take on map.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The pictures on this page are of a device with no project server, so there is&#10;no sync mark on them; the &lt;a href="../sync/"&gt;sync&lt;/a&gt; page shows what one looks like.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Your tags, and a project's tags</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/managing-your-tags/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/managing-your-tags/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A tag is one transmitter: its frequency, pulse modes and name. Which animal&#10;wears it, and since when, is a separate dated record called a deployment, and&#10;a bearing&amp;rsquo;s animal comes from that record.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="diagram"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="diagram-inner" role="img" aria-label="A tag is equipment. An individual is the animal. A deployment is the dated link between them, and it&amp;#39;s what a bearing&amp;#39;s animal actually comes from."&gt;&lt;svg width="228pt" height="361pt"&#10; viewBox="0.00 0.00 228.00 361.00" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="graph0" class="graph" transform="scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(4 357)"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;TagAnimalDeployment&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- tag --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node1" class="node"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;tag&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M170.5,-353C170.5,-353 49.5,-353 49.5,-353 43.5,-353 37.5,-347 37.5,-341 37.5,-341 37.5,-317 37.5,-317 37.5,-311 43.5,-305 49.5,-305 49.5,-305 170.5,-305 170.5,-305 176.5,-305 182.5,-311 182.5,-317 182.5,-317 182.5,-341 182.5,-341 182.5,-347 176.5,-353 170.5,-353"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-332.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Tag&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-318.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;equipment you own&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- deployment --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node2" class="node highlight"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;deployment&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M208,-262C208,-262 12,-262 12,-262 6,-262 0,-256 0,-250 0,-250 0,-226 0,-226 0,-220 6,-214 12,-214 12,-214 208,-214 208,-214 214,-214 220,-220 220,-226 220,-226 220,-250 220,-250 220,-256 214,-262 208,-262"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-241.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Deployment — the dated link&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-227.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;attached_date → removed_date&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- tag&amp;#45;&amp;gt;deployment --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge1" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;tag&amp;#45;&amp;gt;deployment&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M110,-304.62C110,-294.81 110,-283.21 110,-272.52"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="113.5,-272.23 110,-262.23 106.5,-272.23 113.5,-272.23"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- individual --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node3" class="node"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;individual&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M174,-171C174,-171 46,-171 46,-171 40,-171 34,-165 34,-159 34,-159 34,-135 34,-135 34,-129 40,-123 46,-123 46,-123 174,-123 174,-123 180,-123 186,-129 186,-135 186,-135 186,-159 186,-159 186,-165 180,-171 174,-171"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-150.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Individual&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="110" y="-136.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;the animal you study&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- deployment&amp;#45;&amp;gt;individual --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge2" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;deployment&amp;#45;&amp;gt;individual&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M110,-213.62C110,-203.81 110,-192.21 110,-181.52"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="113.5,-181.23 110,-171.23 106.5,-181.23 113.5,-181.23"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- note --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node4" class="node note"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;note&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="none" stroke="black" points="205,-80 9,-80 9,0 211,0 211,-74 205,-80"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polyline fill="none" stroke="black" points="205,-80 205,-74 "/&gt;&#10;&lt;polyline fill="none" stroke="black" points="211,-74 205,-74 "/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="start" x="23" y="-61.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;A bearing gets its animal from the&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="start" x="23" y="-49.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;moment it was taken, not from a&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="start" x="23" y="-37.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;pointer on the tag — it belongs to&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="start" x="23" y="-25.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;whichever deployment&amp;#39;s dates cover&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="start" x="23" y="-13.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;that moment.&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- individual&amp;#45;&amp;gt;note --&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;A tag is equipment. An individual is the animal. A deployment is the dated link between them, and it&amp;#39;s what a bearing&amp;#39;s animal actually comes from.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; has two lists with similar names:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Comparing bearings on the map</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/comparing-bearings-on-the-map/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/comparing-bearings-on-the-map/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Bearings from well-separated spots cross where the animal is, but the Map tab&#10;draws every ray at the same short length. You can drag a ray out to see the&#10;crossing. &lt;em&gt;Nothing on the map says this gesture exists&lt;/em&gt;, so this page is where&#10;it is written down.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="stretch-a-bearing"&gt;Stretch a bearing&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ol&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tap a bearing&lt;/em&gt; (anywhere on the ray, or the small circle at its base) to&#10;select it.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A round handle appears at its tip.&lt;/em&gt; If the tip is off screen, the handle&#10;sits at the last point you can reach.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Press and hold the handle and drag along the line&lt;/em&gt;: out to lengthen, back&#10;to shorten. Sideways movement is ignored, so the heading cannot change.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="shots"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/bearing-selected.png" alt="A bearing tapped and selected. The small round dot at the far end of the ray is the handle; it appears only while a bearing is selected." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;A bearing tapped and selected. The small round dot at the far end of the ray is the handle; it appears only while a bearing is selected.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/bearing-dragged.png" alt="Mid-drag. The ray and its wedge have extended and the readout at the top names the length. The crosshair is not part of the app: it is where the tool that generates these pictures is holding its finger." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;Mid-drag. The ray and its wedge have extended and the readout at the top names the length. The crosshair is not part of the app: it is where the tool that generates these pictures is holding its finger.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;While you drag, the readout shows &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Drawn to&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and the distance.&#10;Stretch several bearings and look where their wedges overlap.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Truth points</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/truth-points/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/truth-points/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A truth point records where somebody physically found the animal, the tag, or&#10;both. It is the yardstick for checking estimates against, so it never feeds an&#10;estimate itself: TriTrack keeps it apart from bearings.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="recording-one"&gt;Recording one&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/record-truth.png" alt="The record screen with the Truth tab chosen. What was found and the precision are the two fields that decide what the point means." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;The record screen with the Truth tab chosen. What was found and the precision are the two fields that decide what the point means.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;On the Record tab, pick &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Truth&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and the tag. Then two fields:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Estimating a position</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/estimating-a-position/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/estimating-a-position/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;With two or more bearings on one tag from different places, the&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Position&lt;/b&gt;&#10; tab estimates where the animal is, with an ellipse for&#10;the uncertainty. It runs on the phone and needs no signal.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/position.png" alt="The Position tab. Every bearing is listed with its time, direction, uncertainty and quality; unticking one recalculates the estimate." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;The Position tab. Every bearing is listed with its time, direction, uncertainty and quality; unticking one recalculates the estimate.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="choose-the-animal"&gt;Choose the animal&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;The bar at the top names the animal, its tag and frequency. Tap it, spin to&#10;another, and tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Select&lt;/b&gt;&#10;. An estimate always uses one tag&amp;rsquo;s&#10;bearings.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sync</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/sync/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/sync/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Everything is recorded on the phone first. Sync sends it to the server and&#10;brings your teammates&amp;rsquo; records back, whenever there is a connection; nothing in&#10;the field waits for it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="diagram"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="diagram-inner" role="img" aria-label="Most records reach the server on the ordinary next sync. A record the server refuses stays safe on this device only; one held back for another reason clears itself once that reason does."&gt;&lt;svg width="323pt" height="476pt"&#10; viewBox="0.00 0.00 322.50 476.00" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="graph0" class="graph" transform="scale(1 1) rotate(0) translate(4 472)"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;SyncStates&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- device --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node1" class="node"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;device&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M123,-468C123,-468 36,-468 36,-468 30,-468 24,-462 24,-456 24,-456 24,-432 24,-432 24,-426 30,-420 36,-420 36,-420 123,-420 123,-420 129,-420 135,-426 135,-432 135,-432 135,-456 135,-456 135,-462 129,-468 123,-468"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-447.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Recorded&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-433.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;on this device&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- waiting --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node2" class="node"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;waiting&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M104,-375C104,-375 55,-375 55,-375 49,-375 43,-369 43,-363 43,-363 43,-339 43,-339 43,-333 49,-327 55,-327 55,-327 104,-327 104,-327 110,-327 116,-333 116,-339 116,-339 116,-363 116,-363 116,-369 110,-375 104,-375"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-354.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Waiting&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-340.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;to sync&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- device&amp;#45;&amp;gt;waiting --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge1" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;device&amp;#45;&amp;gt;waiting&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M79.5,-419.57C79.5,-409.08 79.5,-396.54 79.5,-385.12"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="83,-385.04 79.5,-375.04 76,-385.04 83,-385.04"/&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- stored --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node3" class="node good"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;stored&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M112,-271C112,-271 47,-271 47,-271 41,-271 35,-265 35,-259 35,-259 35,-235 35,-235 35,-229 41,-223 47,-223 47,-223 112,-223 112,-223 118,-223 124,-229 124,-235 124,-235 124,-259 124,-259 124,-265 118,-271 112,-271"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-250.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Stored on&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-236.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;the server&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;stored --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge2" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;stored&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M79.5,-326.85C79.5,-313.42 79.5,-296.27 79.5,-281.4"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="83,-281.05 79.5,-271.05 76,-281.05 83,-281.05"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="121" y="-296.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;the ordinary case&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- refused --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node4" class="node bad"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;refused&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M137.5,-155C137.5,-155 21.5,-155 21.5,-155 15.5,-155 9.5,-149 9.5,-143 9.5,-143 9.5,-119 9.5,-119 9.5,-113 15.5,-107 21.5,-107 21.5,-107 137.5,-107 137.5,-107 143.5,-107 149.5,-113 149.5,-119 149.5,-119 149.5,-143 149.5,-143 149.5,-149 143.5,-155 137.5,-155"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-134.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Refused —&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-120.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;held on this device&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;refused --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge5" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;refused&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M116.2,-342.45C143.21,-334.64 174.32,-319.71 168.5,-293 157.79,-243.79 126.51,-194.13 104.06,-163.23"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="106.75,-160.98 97.99,-155.03 101.13,-165.15 106.75,-160.98"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="196" y="-250.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;the server&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="196" y="-238.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;won&amp;#39;t accept it&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- held --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="node5" class="node wait"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;held&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M147,-62C147,-62 12,-62 12,-62 6,-62 0,-56 0,-50 0,-50 0,-12 0,-12 0,-6 6,0 12,0 12,0 147,0 147,0 153,0 159,-6 159,-12 159,-12 159,-50 159,-50 159,-56 153,-62 147,-62"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-41.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;Held back —&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-27.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;offline, unreadable, or&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="79.5" y="-13.6" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="13.00"&gt;you&amp;#39;re off the project&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;held --&gt;&#10;&lt;g id="edge6" class="edge"&gt;&#10;&lt;title&gt;waiting&amp;#45;&amp;gt;held&lt;/title&gt;&#10;&lt;path fill="none" stroke="black" d="M116.06,-344.06C154.68,-335.53 213.16,-315.61 236.5,-271 275.96,-195.59 192.16,-114 132.49,-68.32"/&gt;&#10;&lt;polygon fill="black" stroke="black" points="134.34,-65.33 124.25,-62.12 130.14,-70.93 134.34,-65.33"/&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="278" y="-192.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;something else&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;text text-anchor="middle" x="278" y="-180.2" font-family="Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif" font-size="11.00"&gt;is stopping it&lt;/text&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- stored&amp;#45;&amp;gt;refused --&gt;&#10;&lt;!-- refused&amp;#45;&amp;gt;held --&gt;&#10;&lt;/g&gt;&#10;&lt;/svg&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;Most records reach the server on the ordinary next sync. A record the server refuses stays safe on this device only; one held back for another reason clears itself once that reason does.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="no-server-is-fine"&gt;No server is fine&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Without a server the app is complete: projects, tags, bearings, estimates, the&#10;map and exports. There is no sync mark and nothing reaches for the network. The&#10;rest of this page applies once a device has a project server and is signed in.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Getting your data out</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/getting-your-data-out/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/docs/getting-your-data-out/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A spreadsheet is for analysis; a backup file moves a whole project or keeps a&#10;second copy of it. Both are under &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; →&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Data Export / Backup&lt;/b&gt;&#10;, and any role, viewers included, can use&#10;both.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="shots"&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/more.png" alt="Data Export / Backup is on the More tab, near the bottom." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;Data Export / Backup is on the More tab, near the bottom.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/data-export.png" alt="Both exports on one screen. The backup is the whole project; the spreadsheet is filtered by tag or by date." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;Both exports on one screen. The backup is the whole project; the spreadsheet is filtered by tag or by date.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="spreadsheets"&gt;Spreadsheets&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Optionally filter by one tag or a date range, then tap&#10;&lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Export CSV&lt;/b&gt;&#10; and choose where to save. You get one zip file named&#10;for the project and the date, holding:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>How it works</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/how-it-works/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/how-it-works/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;One day of tracking, in order, with a link at each step to the full guide page.&#10;The pictures show invented data.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="the-night-before"&gt;The night before&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; → &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Pre-Trip Checklist&lt;/b&gt;&#10;. It shows what the&#10;phone has ready for working without signal, including whether your study&#10;area&amp;rsquo;s map is downloaded. If not, download it now, on wifi. See&#10;&lt;a href="../docs/comparing-bearings-on-the-map/#downloading-map-tiles-for-offline-use"&gt;downloading map tiles&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/checklist.png" alt="The Pre-Trip Checklist: each line is something the phone needs before it loses signal, with what it found." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;The Pre-Trip Checklist: each line is something the phone needs before it loses signal, with what it found.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="take-a-bearing"&gt;Take a bearing&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;On the &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;Record&lt;/b&gt;&#10; tab, spin the wheel to the tag you hear, point the&#10;antenna, and tap &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;POINT&lt;/b&gt;&#10; at the peak or hold &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;RANGE&lt;/b&gt;&#10;&#10;while you sweep across it. Choose the quality and save. Position and time are&#10;filled in for you, and none of it needs a signal. See&#10;&lt;a href="../docs/recording-a-bearing/"&gt;recording a bearing&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Privacy policy</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/privacy/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/privacy/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Most of this policy is not written yet.&lt;/em&gt; It will say what TriTrack stores on&#10;the device, what leaves it when a project syncs to a server, who can read it,&#10;and how long it is kept. Until then, treat nothing here except the section below&#10;as a commitment. For an answer sooner, see &lt;a href="../support/"&gt;Support&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="your-phones-own-backup-and-your-records"&gt;Your phone&amp;rsquo;s own backup, and your records&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This part is written because it is the one thing you might need to act on now.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Support</title><link>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/support/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/support/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Most of this page is not written yet.&lt;/em&gt; It will cover how to report a problem or&#10;ask a question, and what the app does and does not do without a connection.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="which-version-are-you-on"&gt;Which version are you on?&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Open &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;More&lt;/b&gt;&#10; → &lt;b class="app-string"&gt;App Info&lt;/b&gt;&#10;. The first line is the version&#10;and build number; long-press it to copy it into your report.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="shot"&gt;&#10;&lt;img src="https://dynamic-and-active-systems-lab.github.io/tritrack-site/screens/iphone-6.9/app-info.png" alt="App Info. The version at the top is what a bug report needs; below it are the map providers and their licenses." loading="lazy"&gt;&#10;&lt;figcaption&gt;App Info. The version at the top is what a bug report needs; below it are the map providers and their licenses.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10;&lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please include it.&lt;/em&gt; Several builds are in use at once, and a report that cannot&#10;be tied to one gets read against the wrong one. The number is read from the&#10;installed build. If the screen says it could not read the version, say how and&#10;roughly when you installed the app instead.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>